Description: Provides tools for precursor ion purity assessment, processing
    fragmentation data and spectral trees, and spectral matching in
    LC-MSn-based metabolomics. Precursor ion purity estimates the contribution
    of a selected precursor to the signal within its isolation window, using
    neighbouring MS1 measurements for MS2 and linked parent fragmentation
    spectra for higher MSn levels. Fragmentation spectra can be associated
    with chromatographic features, filtered and averaged using acquisition-aware
    settings. Mass Spectral Trees link successive fragmentation spectra, while
    Precursor-Fragment Trees connect individual precursor and product peaks.
    Spectral matching compares measured or consensus spectra with experimental
    spectra and reference libraries, accounting for MS level, precursor
    relationships and acquisition conditions. The optional BLINK method computes
    approximate cosine similarity as described by Harwood et al. (2023)
    <doi:10.1038/s41598-023-40496-9>. Integration with 'Spectra' and 'xcms'
    connects spectrum handling and chromatographic feature information.
    Parquet datasets link raw measurements, processed spectra and reference
    libraries, retaining feature associations, processing settings and
    measurement provenance. Reusable parameter objects and recorded processing
    history support reproducible analysis and reopening of processed results.
    Spectrum selection, linked visualisation, library import and export, and
    reporting of feature information and spectral matches support downstream
    interpretation and data exchange.
